                "Given by Mr and Mrs L.G. Hodson" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/3acd2a57-1697-31d2-8d2f-13553bc38f3f> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This tablecover was donated by the grandson of Laurence Hodson of Compton Hall,  Wolverhampton a great admirer of the work of William Morris who commissioned the firm of Morris & Co. to decorated part of the house. The commission was completed in 1896 and this cloth and related carpet (see T.425-1993) are likely to have been purchased for the house at this time.\n(Registered File number 1993/904)"@en .

